       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't resolve either problem.\n\n- **The dose is unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the 10 mg daily maximum. It could cause profound hypotension and shock, and no patient factor you've described justifies it.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You've told me you're not a clinician, so your confirmation isn't a clinical verification of the dose.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter amlodipine at a standard dose (2.5\u201310 mg by mouth once daily) once you or the prescriber confirm the dose.\n- Enter 50 mg if the treating prescriber gives me the order directly and says they intend that dose. I'd add a note that it was prescriber-verified, and I'd still recommend a pharmacy review.\n- Help you reach the patient's care team or pharmacy if you think something is wrong with the current regimen.\n\nIf the patient needs more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, a clinician would usually add a second agent instead of raising the amlodipine dose."
